Declaration of the adapter method HandlerFunc.Handle: the called function
is the receiver. Its Candidates are every closure converted to HandlerFunc
(the four middlewares and quota's closure), and the middlewares call back
into the adapter (recursion through an interface). Expected: errQuota,
core.ErrDropped, ErrGaveUp, ErrPager, opaque "panic: %v", bare and under
the "%s: %w" / "%w: %w" wraps, truncated at depth 1. Actual: as expected
except for the Recover closure, whose result is unresolved(memory) with
the span "-" (see recover_lit).
-- args --
-chain-depth=1 core/core.go:@hf_handle
